### Note: This file is used to test and validate the Authentication & Session Endpoints.
### It automatically manages secure HttpOnly Refresh Token Cookies across sequential requests.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5165/api
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Account Login
### Authenticates credentials. On success, the server appends a secure HTTP-Only Cookie 
### containing the Refresh Token, which the HTTP Client engine automatically captures.
POST {{baseUrl}}/Auth/LoginAsync
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "userName": "Mohammad",
  "password": "Mohammad1234#"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2. Refresh Security Token Sequence
### Re-evaluates session state. The client engine automatically passes the stored 
### Refresh Token cookie back to the controller endpoint context.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Auth/Refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3. Fetch Current Authenticated User Profile
### Resolves identity from the active principal context claims processing system.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Auth/Current
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4. Account Logout & Session Revocation
### Sends the active cookie payload to revoke token validity inside database state management,
### then instructs the calling agent client to drop and wipe the token cookie entirely.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Auth/Logout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}